  "strategy": "Approach and rationale\nWe seek to improve upon the parent solution by optimizing at multiple grid sizes, from 200 to 900 points. This multi-resolution strategy aims to capture different features that may reduce overlap across shifts. By systematically exploring various discretizations, we can escape local optima common to fixed-grid optimizations while leveraging the parent solution's quality as a warm start.\n\nThe objective remains minimizing C5 = max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx. We maintain hard constraints: 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 and \u222b_0^2 h(x) dx = 1. The evaluation uses circular correlation with finite support matching the supplied `evaluate_erdos_solution` function.\n\nThe key innovation is:\n1) Using interpolation to smoothly transition between grid sizes\n2) Combining SLSQP and focused descent phases\n3) Strict time budget enforcement with warm starts\n\nMathematical specification\nVariables: Step function h on [0,2] defined by grid samples h_i \u2208 [0,1]\nConstraints:\n- Integral constraint: \u2211_{i=1}^n h_i * dx = 1 (dx=2/n)\n- Bounds: 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1\nObjective: C5 = (2/n) * max_{k=-(n-1)}^{n-1} |corr[h, 1-h](k)|\n\nImplementation procedure\n1. Repair parent solution to satisfy constraints\n2. Set grid sizes (n_sizes): [900,800,700,500,400,300,200]\n3. For each grid size:\n   a. Build candidate via parent interpolation\n   b. Apply SLSQP with integrated constraint satisfaction\n   c. Follow with focused descent using top-3 gradient directions\n   d. Repair final solution to enforce constraints\n4. Track best solution (lowest C5) across all grids\n\nSearch choices and variations\n- Grid resolution: [900,800,...,200] (ordered by decreasing n)\n- Optimization sequence: [SLSQP, Focused Descent]\n- Stochastic element: Initial interpolation perturbations\n- Parent utilization: Default to initial_h_values if available\n\nComputational budget and robustness\n- Grid optimization: 200 seconds maximum per grid\n- Fallback: Last repaired parent solution\n- Time checking: Verify elapsed time before SLSQP/Focused Descent\n- Feasibility: Repair ensures integral satisfaction and bounds\n\nValidation and return contract\n- Ensure 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1 and sum(h) * dx = 1\n- Re-evaluate performance using original correlation method\n- Return format: (h_values, c5_bound, n_points)\n- Return checks: Verify finite C5 and non-empty h_values",
